From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:51:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 88/90] linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8250: modem over system sleep

Add kernel 0171-0173: the PCIe host takes the link to the SDX55 down for
system suspend and brings it back on resume, and WAKE# of the modem wakes
the phone. With the link left in L1.2 the modem was gone after a suspend
in which it had to reach the host, for example for an incoming call.
---
 ...Let-only-the-endpoints-decide-about-.patch |  42 +++++
 ..._generic-Make-the-flashless-SDX55-a-.patch |  36 +++++
 ...173-PCI-qcom-Wake-the-system-on-WAKE.patch | 151 ++++++++++++++++++
